30:Tf1c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get from King Khalid International Airport (RUH) to my hotel in Riyadh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Book a private transfer before you fly. Send your flight number, landing time and hotel on WhatsApp, agree the fare, and your driver's contact details are shared before pickup. RUH is about 35 km from central Riyadh — ~30 min on a clear road, longer at weekday commuter peaks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take from RUH to KAFD or Olaya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RUH to the KAFD and Olaya hotel area is about 40 km — ~35 min with clear roads. Morning and late-afternoon commuter peaks can add significantly to that, so departure pickups are planned with a buffer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I hire a private driver in Riyadh for several hours or a full day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Hourly and full-day hire keeps the same car and driver with you, waiting between stops — the usual choice for a business day across KAFD, Olaya and the Diplomatic Quarter, or a shopping and sightseeing day. Send your date, start time and hours needed for a fixed quote."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a private transfer in Riyadh cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The fare depends on the route, vehicle, date and waiting time, so it is quoted per trip and agreed before you book — one fixed price, no meter and no surge, even if the traffic is heavy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What information do I need to send for a quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pickup and drop-off (a hotel name or map pin is ideal), date and time, number of passengers, number of large bags, and your flight number for airport trips. For hourly hire, add the hours and a rough list of stops."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I travel from Riyadh to Dammam, Makkah or Jeddah by private car?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, door to door. Riyadh to Dammam is about 410 km (~4 hr), Riyadh to Makkah about 870 km (~8 hr) and Riyadh to Jeddah about 950 km (~9 hr). Rest and prayer stops are made on request."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I go from Riyadh to Bahrain, Qatar, the UAE or Kuwait by car?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Pre-booked cross-border cars run from Riyadh to Manama (about 450 km via the King Fahd Causeway), Doha, Abu Dhabi, Dubai and Kuwait City. Passengers need their own valid passports and any visas required for entry."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which vehicle should I book for a family with luggage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A full-size SUV fits up to seven passengers with room for several large cases; a VIP van suits a family or group that wants extra luggage space. A sedan is right for one to three people with normal luggage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I pay, and can I get a receipt?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pay the driver in cash or pay by bank transfer. An electronic receipt is available on request — useful for expense claims."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can companies get an invoice for Riyadh transportation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Corporate invoicing can be arranged through our sister company. Email us your company details and trip list for a written quote before booking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I cancel or change my booking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Cancellation is free up to 24 hours before pickup, and you can change times or addresses by WhatsApp."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do the drivers speak English?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Drivers in our Riyadh partner network speak English and Arabic, and trips run 24 hours a day."}}]}29:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$30"}}]
